# Normalize line endings: store LF in the repository, check out the
# platform-native ending (CRLF on Windows, LF on Linux).
#
# Why: this repo is developed on Windows and deployed from Linux (Render).
# Without these rules, every cross-platform edit rewrote whole files in
# `git status`/`git diff`, hiding real changes in line-ending noise.
# The clean filter below converts worktree CRLF to LF before comparison,
# so edits stay content-only no matter which OS made them.
* text=auto

# Windows Task Scheduler scripts must stay CRLF in the worktree — cmd.exe
# label/`goto` handling is unreliable in LF-only batch files.
scripts/*.bat text eol=crlf

# Binary assets: never line-convert or diff.
*.png binary
*.ico binary
*.xlsx binary
*.pdf binary
